  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "k8-dream-compaction-veto",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "K8 keeps a dream intent until its result syncs (#1490). botCompactVeto and the rule compactVeto now refuse a dream intent key with 'The dream result is not synced' until the sync closes that dream, so a compaction that names the key throws CompactVetoError and changes nothing. No Host code change: the caller retries after a later pass, as for a Turn K8 still reads. K8 sealed routine creation and resealing validate Host execution templates with HostOfferSealedPayloadSchema, accepting agentMemoryCommit: on-success-if-advertised (#1506). Hosts can use the conditional option in those templates; cloud enqueue still owns resolution and the device wire is unchanged.",
      "migration": "examples/bot-collaboration/README.md#compaction",
      "items": [
        "example:bot-collaboration"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "agent-memory-commit-if-advertised",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "Host enqueue inputs accept agentMemoryCommit: on-success-if-advertised (#1506). Cloud and embedded server resolve it from the durable device capability declaration before enqueue: on-success when agent-memory-commit-on-success is advertised, otherwise the field is omitted. Literal on-success keeps its strict capability gate. K4 templates retain the Host option and compare replay against the recorded resolution without reading current capabilities. The shared HostOfferPlainPayloadSchema and HostOfferSealedPayloadSchema and their payload types are exported by protocol; the device wire is unchanged. Hosts can replace platform inference with this fixed template option.",
      "migration": "https://github.com/Ancienttwo/byok-sdk/issues/1506",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentDispatchInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentEgressDispatchInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#AgentExecutionInputSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#ByokCloud",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#SealedAgentDispatchInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#SealedAgentEgressDispatchInput",
        "export:@byok-sdk/cloud#SealedAgentExecutionInputSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#HostOfferPlainPayload",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#HostOfferPlainPayloadSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#HostOfferSealedPayload",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#HostOfferSealedPayloadSchema",
        "export:@byok-sdk/server/execution-core#SealedAgentExecutionInput"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "protocol-memory-limits",
      "impact": "additive",
      "summary": "Protocol and its constants entry export AGENT_MEMORY_MAX_FILE_BYTES (256 KiB) and AGENT_MEMORY_MAX_SNAPSHOT_ENTRIES (512) for Host memory prechecks (#1507). The client imports the same limits from protocol and removes both declarations from its reachable internal daemon/agent-memory declaration file; no client package entry exported these names. Existing validation behavior is unchanged.",
      "migration": "https://github.com/Ancienttwo/byok-sdk/issues/1507",
      "items": [
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#AGENT_MEMORY_MAX_FILE_BYTES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol#AGENT_MEMORY_MAX_SNAPSHOT_ENTRIES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol/constants#AGENT_MEMORY_MAX_FILE_BYTES",
        "export:@byok-sdk/protocol/constants#AGENT_MEMORY_MAX_SNAPSHOT_ENTRIES"
      ]
    }
  ],
